  "comments": "This MOR (Mob of Roo&#039;s) coin was introduced by the RAM in May 1984 to replace the $1 Note. It is the only circulation version of the $1 coin to have the Arnold Machin effigy of the Queen, as the 1985 version switched to the Raphael David Maklouf effigy.<br /><br />\r\nThe Uncirculated and Proof sets for 1984 interestingly did not feature a MOR dollar coin.<br />\r\nAn uncirculated version of the MOR was released separately by the RAM in a square red bubble coincard.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d676549775b8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d676549775b8.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"202\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nA Proof version of the 1984 MOR was released separately by the RAM in a blue/grey plush velvet box.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d67655964b47.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d67655964b47.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"209\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nIn 1992 a Re-issue of the coin was released in a five coin set with four other coins unique to the 25mm $1 coin denomination from 1984 to 1992 all with original dates.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd688ccea7e9.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd688ccea7e9.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"139\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd688d730cf6.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd688d730cf6.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"139\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nAn Uncirculated version was also released in a Green Plastic Case Mintage unknown.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dda087f2c2fd.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dda087f2c2fd.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dda0889c8898.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dda0889c8898.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"195\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nIn 2006 The RAM released a Retro Silver Proof version of this coin as part of a 50 Years of Decimal Currency set.",
